<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How much does arbitration cost?</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The costs consist of the fee to the arbitrators/mediator, the administrative fee of the SCC and any expenses incurred.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The SCC determines the costs based on the amount in dispute, which is the total value of all claims, counterclaims and set-offs. This means that the parties often can anticipate the arbitration costs. Use the calculator to estimate such costs.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">When the amount in dispute exceeds EUR 100 000 000 the SCC Board determines the Advance on Costs based on a case by case analysis.</p>

</template>

